# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment branding — every org can run chiku as their own.
# Drop brand assets into static/brand/ (gitignored, served at /brand/…),
# set the vars below in your own .env, and that's it: no code changes, no
# server. A bare clone with none of these shows the shipped default
# ("Chiku" name, Taiga favicon, neutral theme). This whole file is a
# template — copy to .env and keep only what you need.
#
# Full documentation: README.md → "Branding your deployment".
#
# Brand activation — the branding applies when:
#   1. VITE_BRAND=1 (force, handy for previewing on localhost), or
#   2. the hostname matches a suffix in VITE_BRAND_HOSTS (one shared bundle
#      serving several hosts), or
#   3. any brand var below is set and VITE_BRAND_HOSTS is NOT (the normal
#      case: a single-domain deployment).
# BUILD-TIME (VITE_*): rebuild after changing; also restart the dev server.
# Example (workers.vc cohort):
#   VITE_BRAND=1
#   VITE_BRAND_NAME=workers.vc
#   VITE_BRAND_LOGO=/brand/favicon.svg
#   VITE_BRAND_FAVICON=/brand/favicon.svg
#   VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY=oklch(0.55 0.17 145)
#   VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY_DARK=oklch(0.65 0.17 145)
#   VITE_BRAND_HOSTS=workers.vc
#
# Page titles and the og:*/twitter:* tags are baked into the served HTML
# carrying the "chiku | <app name>" prefix; og:image falls back to the logo,
# then the favicon. Crawlers render SVG images poorly, so for crisp link
# previews drop a raster at static/brand/og.png. Set your deployment's public
# origin to get og:url / twitter:url and absolute preview-image URLs:
# VITE_BRAND_OG_IMAGE=
# VITE_BRAND_URL=
# VITE_BRAND_NAME=
# VITE_BRAND_NAME_ACCENT=
# VITE_BRAND_LOGO=
# VITE_BRAND_FAVICON=
# VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY=
# VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY_DARK=
# VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY_FG=
# VITE_BRAND_PRIMARY_DARK_FG=
# VITE_BRAND_HOSTS=



# Taiga API Configuration
# Copy this to .env and set your Taiga backend URL

# For local development with taiga-back running locally:
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1

# For production (your Taiga server):
# VITE_API_URL=https://taiga.yourserver.com/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pie-slicing value units (optional) — the team value and cash tags Chiku
# reads and writes on stories (e.g. "50cook", "100usd", matching mcp-taiga's
# TAG_TEAM/TAG_CASH and GovKit's value_tag_pattern). Unset = cook / usd.
# BUILD-TIME (VITE_*): rebuild after changing.
# VITE_VALUE_UNIT=cook
# VITE_CASH_UNIT=usd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SSO relay (optional) — let a partner app sign a member in through Marten and
# bounce back to itself, so one login covers every team app. The relay route is
# /sso/relay?next=<partner url>; next is honored ONLY if its origin is listed
# here (comma-separated absolute https origins). Unset = relay disabled.
# BUILD-TIME (VITE_*): rebuild after changing.
# Example (workers.vc cohort): VITE_SSO_RELAY_ORIGINS=https://workers.vc
# VITE_SSO_RELAY_ORIGINS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OAuth Configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with LinkedTrust (the team OIDC provider — brokers Google + Bluesky)
# is the primary login and needs NO frontend config: the button sends the
# browser to ${VITE_API_URL}/auth/linkedtrust/redirect and taiga-back runs the
# whole OIDC flow server-side (client_id/secret live in taiga-back), returning
# tokens to {origin}/oauth/callback in the URL fragment.

# Google OAuth - get this from Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials
# Vite exposes only VITE_-prefixed vars to the browser (import.meta.env).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Volunteer-Friendly Role Defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cohort bar (optional) — the cross-app menu workers.vc serves, mounted at the
# top so a person who came from the dash can get back out of the board.
# Unset (the default) mounts nothing; a standalone Marten stays standalone.
# BUILD-TIME (VITE_*): rebuild after changing.
# Example (workers.vc cohort):
# VITE_COHORT_NAV_SRC=https://workers.vc/static/embed/cohort-nav.js

